# Bundler. Gemfile.lock is deliberately not tracked: GitHub Pages ignores it and
# resolves from the version-pinned `github-pages` gem itself, so committing a
# lock only risks pinning transitive gems -- or a `BUNDLED WITH` version -- that
# fights whatever Bundler a contributor happens to have.
Gemfile.lock
.bundle/
vendor/
